<!-- How referrals spread — the image-text layout in slot mode. The picture (`slot="media"`) and the text
     (`slot="body"`) stand side by side, positioned by the theme's image-text.slots.css. The picture is a
     single photo from the deck's `assets/` and becomes a p:pic placeholder in PPTX. `fit="cover"` crops
     around the center to fill the cell — even though the cell's aspect ratio differs per theme, the photo
     never gets empty bands. The radius and shadow of `variant="framed"` belong to the theme.

     The text side is a three-step funnel: share → sign up → first payment. Each step is a big number with a
     short description, and only the last step is `accent3` (the "good number" color in this deck). -->
<slide id="referral" layout="image-text" enter="rise">
  <h2 slot="title">Referrals start on a friend's screen</h2>
  <image slot="media" src="assets/referral.jpg" variant="framed" fit="cover" w="fill" h="400" alt="Two people laughing together over a phone screen in a café"/>
  <col slot="body" gap="lg">
    <row gap="md" align="center">
      <text role="title" size="52" color="accent1" w="150">38%</text>
      <col gap="0" grow="1" basis="0"><text role="heading" size="24">Open the invite link</text><text role="caption">380 of every 1,000 shared links</text></col>
    </row>
    <row gap="md" align="center">
      <text role="title" size="52" color="accent1" w="150">21%</text>
      <col gap="0" grow="1" basis="0"><text role="heading" size="24">Sign up</text><text role="caption">One in five who open — 3x search</text></col>
    </row>
    <row gap="md" align="center">
      <text role="title" size="52" color="accent3" w="150">7.8%</text>
      <col gap="0" grow="1" basis="0"><text role="heading" size="24">Make a first payment</text><text role="caption">Highest conversion of any channel</text></col>
    </row>
  </col>
  <note>A referral isn't an ad, it's a friend talking. That's why conversion is high — and with a reward in place, the cost stays low.</note>
</slide>
